Error [jet.ImpureCallInPureContext]: `bump` writes module state `HITS`
  --> tests/ui/effects/pure_fn_writing_module_state_is_e3401.jet:9:5
    |
  9 |     HITS.value += 1
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Module state outlives the call, so a later call sees the write, but `bump` declares `-[]>`
 Fix: Pass the state in and return the new value, or drop the `-[]>` bound from `bump` so its effects are inferred
 Denial: pure
 Call chain: bump
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3401

